==Trivia==
*The Ururuvu Journals' Japanese name, Ururubutō Taizaiki (ウルルブ島滞在記, "Ururubu Island Travelogue"), is a reference to the Japanese travel show [[wikipedia:ja:世界ウルルン滞在記|''Sekai Ururun Taizaiki'']] (世界ウルルン滞在記, "World Ururun Travelogue"), in which a TV personality has to stay with a local family abroad for a week.
**It may also reference [[wikipedia:JTB Corporation|JTB Publishing]]'s "[[wikipedia:ja:るるぶ|Rurubu]]" travel magazine, the most widely-sold travel guide series in the world.
**It additionally may have been inspired by the South Korean island [[wikipedia:Ulleungdo|Ulleungdo]], whose [[wikipedia:Hanja|Hanja]] name (鬱陵島) can be read as "Ururundō" in Japanese.
*The Ururuvu Journals is the first and currently only sub-chapter to have 4 stages.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Enemy)|Ururun Wolf]] in this sub-chapter is the first enemy in a non-event stage to have separate health and attack magnifications.
*The Ururuvu Journals is comparable to a [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] in that it consists of 4 stages sharing the same boss, with stage 4 having another major threat, [[Mystic Mask Yulala]] (similar to [[Infernal Tyrant Climax (Brutal)|Infernal Tyrant Climax]] having [[M. Ost]], [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|Ghost King Finale]] having [[Kappy Jr.]], [[King of the Beasts: Final Bout (Brutal)|King of the Beasts: Final Bout]] having [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]], etc.).

